There are five types of SQL commands: DDL, DML, DCL, TCL, and DQL.
 
DDL (Data Definition Language):
====================
     It is used to define the database structure or schema such as tables.
    ●DDL is a set of SQL commands used to create, modify, and delete database structures

    ●DDL commands are:
    -------------------
    • CREATE
    • ALTER
    • DROP
    • TRUNCATE

    • CREATE:
    ---------
         This command is used to create the database or its objects (like table, index, function, views, store procedure, and triggers).
        • Syntax: CREATE database database-name; Example for Creating Database, CREATE database Test;
    
    • DROP:
    ---------
     This command is used to delete objects from the database.
        • Syntax: DROP  table table-name; For Example DROP table Student;

    ALTER COMMAND : 
    Alter :
    -------
        Alter command user to modify column information like adding the column dropping the column renaming the column and resizing the column.

        Alter command is used for alteration of table Drop Command There are various uses of alter command, such as: 
        ● to add a column to the existing table .

        ALTER TABLE Student
        ADD age INT;

         ● to rename any existing column.

        ALTER TABLE Student
        RENAME COLUMN name TO student_name;

         ● to change the datatype of any column or to modify its size.

        ALTER TABLE Student
        MODIFY name VARCHAR(100);

        ● alter is also used to drop a column.

        ALTER TABLE Student
        DROP COLUMN age;


    TRUNCATE:
    ----------
        It is used to delete all the rows from the table and free the space containing the table.
        Drop command delete total structure or table of database, 
        Truncate delete all the data in database or rows in database
        Syntax:
        • TRUNCATE TABLE table_name;  
        Example:
        • TRUNCATE TABLE EMPLOYEE;  


2.DML (Data Manipulation Language)
==============================
    ● The DML statements used for managing data within schema objects which deal with data manipulation. 
    ●DML commands are not auto-committed. It means changes are not permanent to the database, they can be rolled back.
    ●Here are some commands that come under DML:
    
    • Insert
    • UPDATE
    • DELETE
    
    ●INSERT COMMAND
    -----------------
     Insert  command  is  used  to  insert  data  into a  table.
    INSERT INTO Student (id, name, age)
    VALUES (1, 'Rahim', 20);

    ●UPDATE COMMAND 
    -----------------
    Update command is used to update a row of a  table. 
    UPDATE Student
    SET age = 21
    WHERE id = 1;
    
    DELETE COMMAND 
    -----------------

    Delete command is used to delete data from a table. Delete command can also be used with conditions to delete a particular row.

    DELETE FROM Student

    DELETE FROM Student
    WHERE id = 1;


